{"record_id": "R13969", "asset_id": "R13969.main.32ca8cbb364b193d", "source_filename": "Pairin_tu_ch3_p.pdf", "source_sha256": "32ca8cbb364b193de87f882ae894fcbc5fef9f26ed5e6f97de81c52c3faf4e30", "canonical_source": "original_files/fulltext/R13969_Pairin_tu_ch3_p.pdf", "role": "main", "location": {"type": "pdf_block", "pdf_page": 1, "pdf_page_label": "", "block": 2, "bbox_points": [117.5, 182.12799072265625, 186.2679901123047, 197.90599060058594]}, "text": "3.1 M aterials\n", "text_method": "native", "chunk_id": "R13969.main.32ca8cbb364b193d:2"}
{"record_id": "R13969", "asset_id": "R13969.main.32ca8cbb364b193d", "source_filename": "Pairin_tu_ch3_p.pdf", "source_sha256": "32ca8cbb364b193de87f882ae894fcbc5fef9f26ed5e6f97de81c52c3faf4e30", "canonical_source": "original_files/fulltext/R13969_Pairin_tu_ch3_p.pdf", "role": "main", "location": {"type": "pdf_block", "pdf_page": 1, "pdf_page_label": "", "block": 3, "bbox_points": [160.19000244140625, 220.1689910888672, 286.7549133300781, 239.92298889160156]}, "text": "3.1.1 Cassava Wastewater\n", "text_method": "native", "chunk_id": "R13969.main.32ca8cbb364b193d:3"}
{"record_id": "R13969", "asset_id": "R13969.main.32ca8cbb364b193d", "source_filename": "Pairin_tu_ch3_p.pdf", "source_sha256": "32ca8cbb364b193de87f882ae894fcbc5fef9f26ed5e6f97de81c52c3faf4e30", "canonical_source": "original_files/fulltext/R13969_Pairin_tu_ch3_p.pdf", "role": "main", "location": {"type": "pdf_block", "pdf_page": 1, "pdf_page_label": "", "block": 4, "bbox_points": [117.49099731445312, 241.0189666748047, 530.7608642578125, 281.6729736328125]}, "text": "The cassava wastewater was screened to remove any large solid \nparticles and used to feed the bioreactor without dilution and addition of any nutrient.\n", "text_method": "native", "chunk_id": "R13969.main.32ca8cbb364b193d:4"}
{"record_id": "R13969", "asset_id": "R13969.main.32ca8cbb364b193d", "source_filename": "Pairin_tu_ch3_p.pdf", "source_sha256": "32ca8cbb364b193de87f882ae894fcbc5fef9f26ed5e6f97de81c52c3faf4e30", "canonical_source": "original_files/fulltext/R13969_Pairin_tu_ch3_p.pdf", "role": "main", "location": {"type": "pdf_block", "pdf_page": 1, "pdf_page_label": "", "block": 5, "bbox_points": [160.19000244140625, 282.5690002441406, 320.55078125, 302.322998046875]}, "text": "3.1.2 Seed Sludge and Substrates\n", "text_method": "native", "chunk_id": "R13969.main.32ca8cbb364b193d:5"}
{"record_id": "R13969", "asset_id": "R13969.main.32ca8cbb364b193d", "source_filename": "Pairin_tu_ch3_p.pdf", "source_sha256": "32ca8cbb364b193de87f882ae894fcbc5fef9f26ed5e6f97de81c52c3faf4e30", "canonical_source": "original_files/fulltext/R13969_Pairin_tu_ch3_p.pdf", "role": "main", "location": {"type": "pdf_block", "pdf_page": 1, "pdf_page_label": "", "block": 6, "bbox_points": [116.739990234375, 303.4189758300781, 530.7607421875, 512.5180053710938]}, "text": "Cassava wastewater was collected from the biogas pant at Ubon \nBiogas Co., Ltd., UbonRatchathani, Thailand.Seed sludge, a full-scale anaerobic \nplant treating cassava wastewater, was collected from SapthipCo., Ltd.,Lopburi, \nThailand. Both seed sludge and cassava wastewater were kept at 4 ๐c before using. \nThe anaerobic seed sludge is black color. A chemical oxygen demand (COD) value \nof the cassava wastewater used in this work was around 14,000mg-L'’, as shown in \nTable 3.1. The ratio of COD:nitrogen:phosphorous was 100:1.43:0.85 which is \nhigher than the theoretical ratio (COD:N:P = 100:1:0.4 for anaerobic decomposition \nfor biogas production (Intanooe/ al., 2012) suggesting that the nitrogen and \nphosphorous contents in the wastewater were sufficient for bacteria growth.\n", "text_method": "native", "chunk_id": "R13969.main.32ca8cbb364b193d:6"}
{"record_id": "R13969", "asset_id": "R13969.main.32ca8cbb364b193d", "source_filename": "Pairin_tu_ch3_p.pdf", "source_sha256": "32ca8cbb364b193de87f882ae894fcbc5fef9f26ed5e6f97de81c52c3faf4e30", "canonical_source": "original_files/fulltext/R13969_Pairin_tu_ch3_p.pdf", "role": "main", "location": {"type": "pdf_block", "pdf_page": 1, "pdf_page_label": "", "block": 7, "bbox_points": [116.49998474121094, 534.5690307617188, 405.97869873046875, 554.322998046875]}, "text": "Table 3.1 Characteristics of the studied cassava wastewater\n", "text_method": "native", "chunk_id": "R13969.main.32ca8cbb364b193d:7"}
{"record_id": "R13969", "asset_id": "R13969.main.32ca8cbb364b193d", "source_filename": "Pairin_tu_ch3_p.pdf", "source_sha256": "32ca8cbb364b193de87f882ae894fcbc5fef9f26ed5e6f97de81c52c3faf4e30", "canonical_source": "original_files/fulltext/R13969_Pairin_tu_ch3_p.pdf", "role": "main", "location": {"type": "pdf_block", "pdf_page": 1, "pdf_page_label": "", "block": 8, "bbox_points": [116.050048828125, 580.2779541015625, 522.5718994140625, 772.9230346679688]}, "text": "Param eters\nUnit\nValue\npH\n-\n4.51\nTotal COD (Total chemical oxygen demand)\nmg-L'1\n14,000\nTotal nitrogen\nmg-L'1\n200.01\nTotal phosphorous\nmg-L\"1\n120\nAmmonium\nmg-L\"1\n2.00\nNitrate\nmg-L-1\n46.48\nNitrite\nmg-L\"1\n1.04\nCOD :N : p\n-\n100 : 1.43 : 0.85\n", "text_method": "native", "chunk_id": "R13969.main.32ca8cbb364b193d:8"}
