{"record_id": "R13969", "asset_id": "R13969.main.32ca8cbb364b193d", "source_filename": "Pairin_tu_ch3_p.pdf", "source_sha256": "32ca8cbb364b193de87f882ae894fcbc5fef9f26ed5e6f97de81c52c3faf4e30", "canonical_source": "original_files/fulltext/R13969_Pairin_tu_ch3_p.pdf", "role": "main", "location": {"type": "pdf_block", "pdf_page": 3, "pdf_page_label": "", "block": 2, "bbox_points": [117.95001220703125, 117.32801055908203, 278.7538757324219, 133.1060028076172]}, "text": "3.3 UASB Setup and Operation\n", "text_method": "native", "chunk_id": "R13969.main.32ca8cbb364b193d:23"}
{"record_id": "R13969", "asset_id": "R13969.main.32ca8cbb364b193d", "source_filename": "Pairin_tu_ch3_p.pdf", "source_sha256": "32ca8cbb364b193de87f882ae894fcbc5fef9f26ed5e6f97de81c52c3faf4e30", "canonical_source": "original_files/fulltext/R13969_Pairin_tu_ch3_p.pdf", "role": "main", "location": {"type": "pdf_block", "pdf_page": 3, "pdf_page_label": "", "block": 3, "bbox_points": [117.94903564453125, 155.5690155029297, 533.089599609375, 300.3699951171875]}, "text": "Each of the upflow anaerobic sludge blanket (UASB) reactors was \nconstructed from borosilicate glass with a 4 and 24 L working volume for hydrogen \nand methane UASB bioreactors, respectively. The operating temperature of both \nreactors was controlled at 37 °c.Moreover, the effluent pH was measured by a pH \nelectrode (Cole-palmer KH-27012-27).The UASB reactors used in this study are \nshown in Figure 3.1. A schematic of the studied two-stage UASB unit used in this \nwork is shown in Figure 3.2.\n", "text_method": "native", "chunk_id": "R13969.main.32ca8cbb364b193d:24"}
{"record_id": "R13969", "asset_id": "R13969.main.32ca8cbb364b193d", "source_filename": "Pairin_tu_ch3_p.pdf", "source_sha256": "32ca8cbb364b193de87f882ae894fcbc5fef9f26ed5e6f97de81c52c3faf4e30", "canonical_source": "original_files/fulltext/R13969_Pairin_tu_ch3_p.pdf", "role": "main", "location": {"type": "pdf_block", "pdf_page": 3, "pdf_page_label": "", "block": 4, "bbox_points": [117.70004272460938, 615.9190063476562, 302.880859375, 635.6729736328125]}, "text": "Figure 3.1 Apparatus of UASB setup.\n", "text_method": "native", "chunk_id": "R13969.main.32ca8cbb364b193d:25"}
{"record_id": "R13969", "asset_id": "R13969.main.32ca8cbb364b193d", "source_filename": "Pairin_tu_ch3_p.pdf", "source_sha256": "32ca8cbb364b193de87f882ae894fcbc5fef9f26ed5e6f97de81c52c3faf4e30", "canonical_source": "original_files/fulltext/R13969_Pairin_tu_ch3_p.pdf", "role": "main", "location": {"type": "pdf_block", "pdf_page": 3, "pdf_page_label": "", "block": 5, "bbox_points": [117.50004577636719, 657.4190063476562, 533.319580078125, 781.5700073242188]}, "text": "The cassava wastewater was pumped into the bottom of the hydrogen production \nreactor and was flown up through the flocculants of microorganisms.The organic \ncompounds in the feed, especially carbohydrates, were digested by the \nmicroorganisms, and gaseous products weregenerated.Athree-phase separator was \nused to prevent an outflow of flocculants, to collect the gaseous products, and to \ncollect the overflown liquid effluent to the mixing tank. The pH of the effluent from\n", "text_method": "native", "chunk_id": "R13969.main.32ca8cbb364b193d:26"}
{"record_id": "R13969", "asset_id": "R13969.main.32ca8cbb364b193d", "source_filename": "Pairin_tu_ch3_p.pdf", "source_sha256": "32ca8cbb364b193de87f882ae894fcbc5fef9f26ed5e6f97de81c52c3faf4e30", "canonical_source": "original_files/fulltext/R13969_Pairin_tu_ch3_p.pdf", "role": "main", "location": {"type": "pdf_block", "pdf_page": 3, "pdf_page_label": "", "block": 6, "bbox_points": [91.550048828125, 808.8400268554688, 96.50004577636719, 825.7450561523438]}, "text": "o\n", "text_method": "native", "chunk_id": "R13969.main.32ca8cbb364b193d:27"}
{"record_id": "R13969", "asset_id": "R13969.main.32ca8cbb364b193d", "source_filename": "Pairin_tu_ch3_p.pdf", "source_sha256": "32ca8cbb364b193de87f882ae894fcbc5fef9f26ed5e6f97de81c52c3faf4e30", "canonical_source": "original_files/fulltext/R13969_Pairin_tu_ch3_p.pdf", "role": "main", "location": {"type": "pdf_block", "pdf_page": 4, "pdf_page_label": "", "block": 1, "bbox_points": [516.7999877929688, 37.70197296142578, 527.4720458984375, 56.29397201538086]}, "text": "30\n", "text_method": "native", "chunk_id": "R13969.main.32ca8cbb364b193d:28"}
{"record_id": "R13969", "asset_id": "R13969.main.32ca8cbb364b193d", "source_filename": "Pairin_tu_ch3_p.pdf", "source_sha256": "32ca8cbb364b193de87f882ae894fcbc5fef9f26ed5e6f97de81c52c3faf4e30", "canonical_source": "original_files/fulltext/R13969_Pairin_tu_ch3_p.pdf", "role": "main", "location": {"type": "pdf_block", "pdf_page": 4, "pdf_page_label": "", "block": 2, "bbox_points": [116.25, 115.7289810180664, 530.6246337890625, 239.6800079345703]}, "text": "the hydrogen production reactor was controlled at 5.5, and this pH-controlled \neffluent was fed as a feed substrate into the methane production reactor without \nfurther pH control.In the first part, cassava wastewater was digested in the anaerobic \ndigestion without oxygen supply. The COD loading rate was varied from 12 to 60 \nkg-m‘3 d'1corresponding to the feed flow rate and hydraulic retention time (HRT) \nshown in Table 3.2 to determine the optimum COD loading rate.\n", "text_method": "native", "chunk_id": "R13969.main.32ca8cbb364b193d:29"}
{"record_id": "R13969", "asset_id": "R13969.main.32ca8cbb364b193d", "source_filename": "Pairin_tu_ch3_p.pdf", "source_sha256": "32ca8cbb364b193de87f882ae894fcbc5fef9f26ed5e6f97de81c52c3faf4e30", "canonical_source": "original_files/fulltext/R13969_Pairin_tu_ch3_p.pdf", "role": "main", "location": {"type": "pdf_block", "pdf_page": 4, "pdf_page_label": "", "block": 3, "bbox_points": [115.30000305175781, 530.4790649414062, 511.7705078125, 550.2330322265625]}, "text": "Figure 3.2 Schematic of two stage upflow anaerobic sludge blanket (UASB) unit.\n", "text_method": "native", "chunk_id": "R13969.main.32ca8cbb364b193d:30"}
{"record_id": "R13969", "asset_id": "R13969.main.32ca8cbb364b193d", "source_filename": "Pairin_tu_ch3_p.pdf", "source_sha256": "32ca8cbb364b193de87f882ae894fcbc5fef9f26ed5e6f97de81c52c3faf4e30", "canonical_source": "original_files/fulltext/R13969_Pairin_tu_ch3_p.pdf", "role": "main", "location": {"type": "pdf_block", "pdf_page": 4, "pdf_page_label": "", "block": 4, "bbox_points": [114.79998779296875, 572.4790649414062, 529.8887329101562, 655.58203125]}, "text": "Table 3.2 COD loading rate, flow rate, and hydraulic retention time (HRT) for \ndetermining the effect of COD loading rate on hydrogen UASB volume at pH 5.5 \nand on methane UASB volume without pH controlled under mesophilic temperature \n(COD = 14 g-L'1)\n", "text_method": "native", "chunk_id": "R13969.main.32ca8cbb364b193d:31"}
