{"record_id": "R13969", "asset_id": "R13969.main.32ca8cbb364b193d", "source_filename": "Pairin_tu_ch3_p.pdf", "source_sha256": "32ca8cbb364b193de87f882ae894fcbc5fef9f26ed5e6f97de81c52c3faf4e30", "canonical_source": "original_files/fulltext/R13969_Pairin_tu_ch3_p.pdf", "role": "main", "location": {"type": "pdf_block", "pdf_page": 5, "pdf_page_label": "", "block": 7, "bbox_points": [118.19999694824219, 584.35400390625, 339.02996826171875, 603.5130004882812]}, "text": "3.4 Measurements and Analytical Methods\n", "text_method": "native", "chunk_id": "R13969.main.32ca8cbb364b193d:39"}
{"record_id": "R13969", "asset_id": "R13969.main.32ca8cbb364b193d", "source_filename": "Pairin_tu_ch3_p.pdf", "source_sha256": "32ca8cbb364b193de87f882ae894fcbc5fef9f26ed5e6f97de81c52c3faf4e30", "canonical_source": "original_files/fulltext/R13969_Pairin_tu_ch3_p.pdf", "role": "main", "location": {"type": "pdf_block", "pdf_page": 5, "pdf_page_label": "", "block": 8, "bbox_points": [160.44000244140625, 625.009033203125, 270.5798034667969, 665.6629638671875]}, "text": "3.4.1 COD Analysis \n3.4.1.1 Reagents\n", "text_method": "native", "chunk_id": "R13969.main.32ca8cbb364b193d:40"}
{"record_id": "R13969", "asset_id": "R13969.main.32ca8cbb364b193d", "source_filename": "Pairin_tu_ch3_p.pdf", "source_sha256": "32ca8cbb364b193de87f882ae894fcbc5fef9f26ed5e6f97de81c52c3faf4e30", "canonical_source": "original_files/fulltext/R13969_Pairin_tu_ch3_p.pdf", "role": "main", "location": {"type": "pdf_block", "pdf_page": 5, "pdf_page_label": "", "block": 9, "bbox_points": [117.95001220703125, 667.259033203125, 532.31982421875, 749.4119873046875]}, "text": "- Digestion solution. 10.216 g of dried K.2Cr207 (primary \nstandard grade), 167 ml of 98% H2SO4, and 33.3 g of HgS04 were added into 500 ml \ndistilled water. Then the mixture was left for complete dissolution, cooled to room \ntemperature, and finally diluted to 1 L.\n", "text_method": "native", "chunk_id": "R13969.main.32ca8cbb364b193d:41"}
{"record_id": "R13969", "asset_id": "R13969.main.32ca8cbb364b193d", "source_filename": "Pairin_tu_ch3_p.pdf", "source_sha256": "32ca8cbb364b193de87f882ae894fcbc5fef9f26ed5e6f97de81c52c3faf4e30", "canonical_source": "original_files/fulltext/R13969_Pairin_tu_ch3_p.pdf", "role": "main", "location": {"type": "pdf_block", "pdf_page": 6, "pdf_page_label": "", "block": 1, "bbox_points": [518.0, 38.23200225830078, 528.56005859375, 56.82400131225586]}, "text": "32\n", "text_method": "native", "chunk_id": "R13969.main.32ca8cbb364b193d:42"}
{"record_id": "R13969", "asset_id": "R13969.main.32ca8cbb364b193d", "source_filename": "Pairin_tu_ch3_p.pdf", "source_sha256": "32ca8cbb364b193de87f882ae894fcbc5fef9f26ed5e6f97de81c52c3faf4e30", "canonical_source": "original_files/fulltext/R13969_Pairin_tu_ch3_p.pdf", "role": "main", "location": {"type": "pdf_block", "pdf_page": 6, "pdf_page_label": "", "block": 2, "bbox_points": [118.15000915527344, 116.2590103149414, 531.8660888671875, 177.3130645751953]}, "text": "- Sulfuric acid reagent. Ag2SC>4 (reagent grade, crystals or \npowder) was added to 98% H2SO4. The mixture was left to stand for 1 to 2 d to \ncompletely dissolve the Ag2SC>4.\n", "text_method": "native", "chunk_id": "R13969.main.32ca8cbb364b193d:43"}
{"record_id": "R13969", "asset_id": "R13969.main.32ca8cbb364b193d", "source_filename": "Pairin_tu_ch3_p.pdf", "source_sha256": "32ca8cbb364b193de87f882ae894fcbc5fef9f26ed5e6f97de81c52c3faf4e30", "canonical_source": "original_files/fulltext/R13969_Pairin_tu_ch3_p.pdf", "role": "main", "location": {"type": "pdf_block", "pdf_page": 6, "pdf_page_label": "", "block": 3, "bbox_points": [188.0, 178.40904235839844, 279.61285400390625, 198.1630401611328]}, "text": "3.4.1.2 Procedure\n", "text_method": "native", "chunk_id": "R13969.main.32ca8cbb364b193d:44"}
{"record_id": "R13969", "asset_id": "R13969.main.32ca8cbb364b193d", "source_filename": "Pairin_tu_ch3_p.pdf", "source_sha256": "32ca8cbb364b193de87f882ae894fcbc5fef9f26ed5e6f97de81c52c3faf4e30", "canonical_source": "original_files/fulltext/R13969_Pairin_tu_ch3_p.pdf", "role": "main", "location": {"type": "pdf_block", "pdf_page": 6, "pdf_page_label": "", "block": 4, "bbox_points": [117.71000671386719, 199.05906677246094, 531.4517822265625, 364.75909423828125]}, "text": "Adilute sample of 2.5 ml was added to a digestion vial \n(HACH, 16x100 mm).Thedigestion reagent of 1.5 ml was added to the vial. \nAfterwards, sulfuric acid reagent was slowly dropped for 3.5 ml into the vial.The vial \nwas inverted several times to homogeneously mix the contents and heated for 2 h in \nthe preheated COD reactor (HACH, DR3800) shown in Figure 3.3a.After that,the \nvial was cooled to room temperature. Lastly, it was placed into the \nspectrophotometer (HACH, DRB200)for reading COD value, as shown in Figure \n3.3b.\n", "text_method": "native", "chunk_id": "R13969.main.32ca8cbb364b193d:45"}
{"record_id": "R13969", "asset_id": "R13969.main.32ca8cbb364b193d", "source_filename": "Pairin_tu_ch3_p.pdf", "source_sha256": "32ca8cbb364b193de87f882ae894fcbc5fef9f26ed5e6f97de81c52c3faf4e30", "canonical_source": "original_files/fulltext/R13969_Pairin_tu_ch3_p.pdf", "role": "main", "location": {"type": "pdf_block", "pdf_page": 6, "pdf_page_label": "", "block": 5, "bbox_points": [117.69999694824219, 533.4091186523438, 380.7386169433594, 553.1630859375]}, "text": "Figure 3.3 (a)COD reactor and (b) spectrophotometer.\n", "text_method": "native", "chunk_id": "R13969.main.32ca8cbb364b193d:46"}
{"record_id": "R13969", "asset_id": "R13969.main.32ca8cbb364b193d", "source_filename": "Pairin_tu_ch3_p.pdf", "source_sha256": "32ca8cbb364b193de87f882ae894fcbc5fef9f26ed5e6f97de81c52c3faf4e30", "canonical_source": "original_files/fulltext/R13969_Pairin_tu_ch3_p.pdf", "role": "main", "location": {"type": "pdf_block", "pdf_page": 6, "pdf_page_label": "", "block": 6, "bbox_points": [159.19000244140625, 575.1591186523438, 397.5298156738281, 594.9130859375]}, "text": "3.4.2 Total VFA and VFA Composition Analysis\n", "text_method": "native", "chunk_id": "R13969.main.32ca8cbb364b193d:47"}
{"record_id": "R13969", "asset_id": "R13969.main.32ca8cbb364b193d", "source_filename": "Pairin_tu_ch3_p.pdf", "source_sha256": "32ca8cbb364b193de87f882ae894fcbc5fef9f26ed5e6f97de81c52c3faf4e30", "canonical_source": "original_files/fulltext/R13969_Pairin_tu_ch3_p.pdf", "role": "main", "location": {"type": "pdf_block", "pdf_page": 6, "pdf_page_label": "", "block": 7, "bbox_points": [117.20098876953125, 596.2590942382812, 531.7184448242188, 763.1260986328125]}, "text": "The amount of VFAs in mg as acetic per liter and VFAs composition \nwere analyzed by a high-perfonnance liquid chromatography (HPLC), UFLC \nshimadzu equipped with a refractive index detector(RID detector). An HPLC \ninstrument consists of 0.004 M of sulfuric acid which used to be mobile phase, \ndeionized water(DI) filtrated by paper filter 0.45 micron used to bea solvent pump, \nand arefractive index detector used, all connected by tubing. Samples are injected \ninto a stream of solvent being pumped through the column at flow rate 0.5 mL-min\"1 \nunder temperature 45 °c by using columnof Cl 8. While passing through the column,\n", "text_method": "native", "chunk_id": "R13969.main.32ca8cbb364b193d:48"}
{"record_id": "R13969", "asset_id": "R13969.main.32ca8cbb364b193d", "source_filename": "Pairin_tu_ch3_p.pdf", "source_sha256": "32ca8cbb364b193de87f882ae894fcbc5fef9f26ed5e6f97de81c52c3faf4e30", "canonical_source": "original_files/fulltext/R13969_Pairin_tu_ch3_p.pdf", "role": "main", "location": {"type": "pdf_block", "pdf_page": 6, "pdf_page_label": "", "block": 8, "bbox_points": [562.1499633789062, 805.5320434570312, 568.5819702148438, 824.1240234375]}, "text": "๐\n", "text_method": "native", "chunk_id": "R13969.main.32ca8cbb364b193d:49"}
{"record_id": "R13969", "asset_id": "R13969.main.32ca8cbb364b193d", "source_filename": "Pairin_tu_ch3_p.pdf", "source_sha256": "32ca8cbb364b193de87f882ae894fcbc5fef9f26ed5e6f97de81c52c3faf4e30", "canonical_source": "original_files/fulltext/R13969_Pairin_tu_ch3_p.pdf", "role": "main", "location": {"type": "pdf_block", "pdf_page": 7, "pdf_page_label": "", "block": 1, "bbox_points": [515.2000122070312, 37.66199493408203, 525.3760986328125, 56.25399398803711]}, "text": "33\n", "text_method": "native", "chunk_id": "R13969.main.32ca8cbb364b193d:50"}
{"record_id": "R13969", "asset_id": "R13969.main.32ca8cbb364b193d", "source_filename": "Pairin_tu_ch3_p.pdf", "source_sha256": "32ca8cbb364b193de87f882ae894fcbc5fef9f26ed5e6f97de81c52c3faf4e30", "canonical_source": "original_files/fulltext/R13969_Pairin_tu_ch3_p.pdf", "role": "main", "location": {"type": "pdf_block", "pdf_page": 7, "pdf_page_label": "", "block": 2, "bbox_points": [114.90000915527344, 115.4889907836914, 528.5269165039062, 156.0929718017578]}, "text": "the analysts separate from one another. When they exit the column, a RID detector \nproduces a signal proportional to the amount of each analyst.\n", "text_method": "native", "chunk_id": "R13969.main.32ca8cbb364b193d:51"}
{"record_id": "R13969", "asset_id": "R13969.main.32ca8cbb364b193d", "source_filename": "Pairin_tu_ch3_p.pdf", "source_sha256": "32ca8cbb364b193de87f882ae894fcbc5fef9f26ed5e6f97de81c52c3faf4e30", "canonical_source": "original_files/fulltext/R13969_Pairin_tu_ch3_p.pdf", "role": "main", "location": {"type": "pdf_block", "pdf_page": 7, "pdf_page_label": "", "block": 3, "bbox_points": [157.10000610351562, 157.23899841308594, 313.9707946777344, 176.9929962158203]}, "text": "3.4.3 Gas Composition Analysis\n", "text_method": "native", "chunk_id": "R13969.main.32ca8cbb364b193d:52"}
{"record_id": "R13969", "asset_id": "R13969.main.32ca8cbb364b193d", "source_filename": "Pairin_tu_ch3_p.pdf", "source_sha256": "32ca8cbb364b193de87f882ae894fcbc5fef9f26ed5e6f97de81c52c3faf4e30", "canonical_source": "original_files/fulltext/R13969_Pairin_tu_ch3_p.pdf", "role": "main", "location": {"type": "pdf_block", "pdf_page": 7, "pdf_page_label": "", "block": 4, "bbox_points": [114.63900756835938, 178.33897399902344, 528.500732421875, 281.14093017578125]}, "text": "The gas composition was determined by a gas chromatograph \n(AutoSystem GC, Perkin-Elmer) equipped with a thermal conductivity detector \n(TCD) and a stainless-steel 10' X 1/8\" X .085\" HayeSep D 100/120 mesh (Alltech) \npacked column. Injector and detector temperatures were kept at 60, 35, and 150 ๐c, \nrespectively. Argon was used as the carrier gas at pressure of 345 kPa.\n", "text_method": "native", "chunk_id": "R13969.main.32ca8cbb364b193d:53"}
{"record_id": "R13969", "asset_id": "R13969.main.32ca8cbb364b193d", "source_filename": "Pairin_tu_ch3_p.pdf", "source_sha256": "32ca8cbb364b193de87f882ae894fcbc5fef9f26ed5e6f97de81c52c3faf4e30", "canonical_source": "original_files/fulltext/R13969_Pairin_tu_ch3_p.pdf", "role": "main", "location": {"type": "pdf_block", "pdf_page": 7, "pdf_page_label": "", "block": 5, "bbox_points": [156.6500244140625, 282.2889099121094, 293.24481201171875, 302.04290771484375]}, "text": "3.4.4 Phosphorous Analysis\n", "text_method": "native", "chunk_id": "R13969.main.32ca8cbb364b193d:54"}
{"record_id": "R13969", "asset_id": "R13969.main.32ca8cbb364b193d", "source_filename": "Pairin_tu_ch3_p.pdf", "source_sha256": "32ca8cbb364b193de87f882ae894fcbc5fef9f26ed5e6f97de81c52c3faf4e30", "canonical_source": "original_files/fulltext/R13969_Pairin_tu_ch3_p.pdf", "role": "main", "location": {"type": "pdf_block", "pdf_page": 7, "pdf_page_label": "", "block": 6, "bbox_points": [114.39102172851562, 303.3888854980469, 528.5947265625, 385.04193115234375]}, "text": "The total phosphorous in feed and effluent samples was determined by \nthe molybdovanadate method with acid persulfate digestion (Hach Company). The \nsample cell was placed into the spectrophotometer (HACH DRB200)for determining \nphosphorous content.\n", "text_method": "native", "chunk_id": "R13969.main.32ca8cbb364b193d:55"}
{"record_id": "R13969", "asset_id": "R13969.main.32ca8cbb364b193d", "source_filename": "Pairin_tu_ch3_p.pdf", "source_sha256": "32ca8cbb364b193de87f882ae894fcbc5fef9f26ed5e6f97de81c52c3faf4e30", "canonical_source": "original_files/fulltext/R13969_Pairin_tu_ch3_p.pdf", "role": "main", "location": {"type": "pdf_block", "pdf_page": 7, "pdf_page_label": "", "block": 7, "bbox_points": [156.1500244140625, 386.1889343261719, 273.466796875, 405.94293212890625]}, "text": "3.4.5 Nitrogen Analysis\n", "text_method": "native", "chunk_id": "R13969.main.32ca8cbb364b193d:56"}
{"record_id": "R13969", "asset_id": "R13969.main.32ca8cbb364b193d", "source_filename": "Pairin_tu_ch3_p.pdf", "source_sha256": "32ca8cbb364b193de87f882ae894fcbc5fef9f26ed5e6f97de81c52c3faf4e30", "canonical_source": "original_files/fulltext/R13969_Pairin_tu_ch3_p.pdf", "role": "main", "location": {"type": "pdf_block", "pdf_page": 7, "pdf_page_label": "", "block": 8, "bbox_points": [113.90103149414062, 407.2889099121094, 528.1546020507812, 510.58984375]}, "text": "The nitrogen concentrations (in terms of organic-nitrogen by the \ndiazotization, and cadmium reduction method and inorganic nitrogen by the \nsalicylate method) in feed and effluent samples were carried out with the TNT \npersulfate digestion. The sample cell was placed into the spectrophotometer (HACH \nDRB200) for determining nitrogen content.\n", "text_method": "native", "chunk_id": "R13969.main.32ca8cbb364b193d:57"}
{"record_id": "R13969", "asset_id": "R13969.main.32ca8cbb364b193d", "source_filename": "Pairin_tu_ch3_p.pdf", "source_sha256": "32ca8cbb364b193de87f882ae894fcbc5fef9f26ed5e6f97de81c52c3faf4e30", "canonical_source": "original_files/fulltext/R13969_Pairin_tu_ch3_p.pdf", "role": "main", "location": {"type": "pdf_block", "pdf_page": 7, "pdf_page_label": "", "block": 9, "bbox_points": [113.70001220703125, 512.1889038085938, 554.5670776367188, 700.1568603515625]}, "text": "3.4.6 Microbial Concentration (MLVSS) \n\"\nThe microbial concentration in the system, which is a parameter for\ndetermining the degradation of organic compounds present in the reactor, can be \nmeasured in terms of microbial concentration or MLVSS. At steady state, the whole \nliquid and solid components are drained out from the reactor and then stirred with a \nstirrer until homogeneous mixing. The collected sample was filtrated through a glass \nfiber filter, washed with distilled water, and dried in an oven at 105 °c for 1 h. The \ndried residue sample is determined for MLSS. The MLVSS is the difference between \nthe dried residue sample at 105 °c and the dried residue sample at 550 °c (for 1 h.).\n", "text_method": "native", "chunk_id": "R13969.main.32ca8cbb364b193d:58"}
{"record_id": "R13969", "asset_id": "R13969.main.32ca8cbb364b193d", "source_filename": "Pairin_tu_ch3_p.pdf", "source_sha256": "32ca8cbb364b193de87f882ae894fcbc5fef9f26ed5e6f97de81c52c3faf4e30", "canonical_source": "original_files/fulltext/R13969_Pairin_tu_ch3_p.pdf", "role": "main", "location": {"type": "pdf_block", "pdf_page": 7, "pdf_page_label": "", "block": 10, "bbox_points": [155.44000244140625, 700.5888671875, 352.92877197265625, 720.3428344726562]}, "text": "3.4.7 Microbial Washout (Effluent VSS)\n", "text_method": "native", "chunk_id": "R13969.main.32ca8cbb364b193d:59"}
{"record_id": "R13969", "asset_id": "R13969.main.32ca8cbb364b193d", "source_filename": "Pairin_tu_ch3_p.pdf", "source_sha256": "32ca8cbb364b193de87f882ae894fcbc5fef9f26ed5e6f97de81c52c3faf4e30", "canonical_source": "original_files/fulltext/R13969_Pairin_tu_ch3_p.pdf", "role": "main", "location": {"type": "pdf_block", "pdf_page": 7, "pdf_page_label": "", "block": 11, "bbox_points": [113.70100402832031, 721.6889038085938, 529.099853515625, 783.4418334960938]}, "text": "The microbial washout from the system can be measured in terms of \nEffluent VSS. At steady state, the effluent liquid and solid components are drained \nout from the reactor. The collected sample was filtrated through a glass fiber filter,\n", "text_method": "native", "chunk_id": "R13969.main.32ca8cbb364b193d:60"}
{"record_id": "R13969", "asset_id": "R13969.main.32ca8cbb364b193d", "source_filename": "Pairin_tu_ch3_p.pdf", "source_sha256": "32ca8cbb364b193de87f882ae894fcbc5fef9f26ed5e6f97de81c52c3faf4e30", "canonical_source": "original_files/fulltext/R13969_Pairin_tu_ch3_p.pdf", "role": "main", "location": {"type": "pdf_block", "pdf_page": 7, "pdf_page_label": "", "block": 12, "bbox_points": [395.20001220703125, 805.6618041992188, 401.63201904296875, 824.2537841796875]}, "text": "๐\n", "text_method": "native", "chunk_id": "R13969.main.32ca8cbb364b193d:61"}
{"record_id": "R13969", "asset_id": "R13969.main.32ca8cbb364b193d", "source_filename": "Pairin_tu_ch3_p.pdf", "source_sha256": "32ca8cbb364b193de87f882ae894fcbc5fef9f26ed5e6f97de81c52c3faf4e30", "canonical_source": "original_files/fulltext/R13969_Pairin_tu_ch3_p.pdf", "role": "main", "location": {"type": "pdf_block", "pdf_page": 8, "pdf_page_label": "", "block": 1, "bbox_points": [517.3499755859375, 37.42200469970703, 528.0220336914062, 56.01400375366211]}, "text": "34\n", "text_method": "native", "chunk_id": "R13969.main.32ca8cbb364b193d:62"}
{"record_id": "R13969", "asset_id": "R13969.main.32ca8cbb364b193d", "source_filename": "Pairin_tu_ch3_p.pdf", "source_sha256": "32ca8cbb364b193de87f882ae894fcbc5fef9f26ed5e6f97de81c52c3faf4e30", "canonical_source": "original_files/fulltext/R13969_Pairin_tu_ch3_p.pdf", "role": "main", "location": {"type": "pdf_block", "pdf_page": 8, "pdf_page_label": "", "block": 2, "bbox_points": [116.53005981445312, 114.9990005493164, 530.7272338867188, 176.5020294189453]}, "text": "washed with distilled water, and dried in an oven at 105 °c for 1 h. The dried residue \nsample was determined for TSS. The effluent v s s  is the difference between the \ndried residue sample at 105 °c and the dried residue sample at 550 °c (for 1 h.).\n", "text_method": "native", "chunk_id": "R13969.main.32ca8cbb364b193d:63"}
{"record_id": "R13969", "asset_id": "R13969.main.32ca8cbb364b193d", "source_filename": "Pairin_tu_ch3_p.pdf", "source_sha256": "32ca8cbb364b193de87f882ae894fcbc5fef9f26ed5e6f97de81c52c3faf4e30", "canonical_source": "original_files/fulltext/R13969_Pairin_tu_ch3_p.pdf", "role": "main", "location": {"type": "pdf_block", "pdf_page": 8, "pdf_page_label": "", "block": 3, "bbox_points": [230.800048828125, 807.8200073242188, 235.7500457763672, 824.7250366210938]}, "text": "o\n", "text_method": "native", "chunk_id": "R13969.main.32ca8cbb364b193d:64"}
